    arm64: dts: apple: t8122-j613: Wire dcpext to the left-front USB-C port too
    
    Give dcpext a second Type-C display route, to the left-front port
    (typec1, ATC1): ATC1's DP PHY and display crossbar as typec1, the same
    crossbar state as the left-back port (2, dispext1,0: one display pipe
    behind either ATC's crossbar), DPTX target 1 (the ADT's DFP index of
    atc1, as in the M1/M2 dcpext routes), and port@3 on the front connector.
    Enable ATC1's crossbar and keep ATC1's common power state on, as for
    ATC0.
    
    route@1 stays disabled like route@0; the display gate enables every
    route of the dcpext together with it. dcpext has one DPTX link, so one
    external display at a time: the display fabric gives the pipeline to the
    first port that asks, and a DP partner on the other port gets USB only.
    
    Tested on J613 with the same route added at boot by the display gate
    instead of the device tree (identical properties): picture, hotplug and
    DPMS on the front port, USB on the other port in both arrangements.
    
    Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
